    <ferc:StatementAboutImportantChangesDuringTheQuarterYearTextBlock id="f-395" contextRef="c-08">&lt;p&gt;1. Not Applicable&lt;br /&gt;2. Not Applicable&lt;br /&gt;3. Not Applicable&lt;br /&gt;4. Not Applicable&lt;br /&gt;5. Not Applicable&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</ferc:StatementAboutImportantChangesDuringTheQuarterYearTextBlock>
    <ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="f-397" contextRef="c-08">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); line-height: normal"&gt;&lt;span lang="en-US" style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; text-decoration: none"&gt;NOTE A - ORGANIZATION, OPERATIONS, AND BASIS OF PRESENTATION:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); line-height: normal"&gt;&lt;span lang="en-US" style="background-color: initial; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-weight: bold; line-height: 14.2667px"&gt;&lt;br style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small" /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); line-height: normal"&gt;&lt;span lang="en-US" style="background-color: initial; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-weight: bold; line-height: 14.2667px"&gt;Organization. &lt;/span&gt;P&lt;span lang="en-US" style="background-color: initial; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; line-height: 14.2667px"&gt;ermian Express Partners LLC (&amp;quot;PEP&amp;quot;) is a joint venture, owned 88% by ET CC Holdings LLC (&amp;quot;ET CC&amp;quot;), a wholly owned subsidiary of Energy Transfer LP (&amp;quot;Energy Transfer&amp;quot;), and 12% by Mid-Point Pipeline LLC (which is owned by ExxonMobil Pipeline Company (&amp;quot;ExxonMobil&amp;quot;)). ET CC maintains a controlling financial and voting interest in PEP and is the operator of PEP. PEP owns a 40% membership interest in Bakken Holdings Company LLC and a 100% membership interest in Permian Express Partners Operating LLC.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); line-height: normal"&gt;&lt;span lang="en-US" style="background-color: initial; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; line-height: 14.2667px"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span lang="en-US" style="background-color: initial; text-align: inherit; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-weight: bold; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;Operations.&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="background-color: initial; text-align: inherit; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;P&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span lang="en-US" style="background-color: initial; text-align: inherit; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;EP is a Delaware limited liability company engaged in the transportation of crude oil.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); line-height: normal"&gt;&lt;span lang="en-US" style="background-color: initial; text-align: inherit; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); line-height: normal"&gt;&lt;span lang="en-US" style="font-weight: bold; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;Regulation.&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;P&lt;span lang="en-US" style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;EP's crude oil transportation activities are subject to regulation by the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission (&amp;quot;FERC&amp;quot;) and various state authorities. Regulatory bodies exercise statutory authority over matters such as rates, underlying accounting practices, and rate-making agreements with customers.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); line-height: normal"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); line-height: normal"&gt;&lt;span lang="en-US" style="font-weight: bold; line-height: 14.2667px; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;Basis of Presentation.&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;T&lt;span lang="en-US" style="line-height: 14.2667px; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;he f&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span lang="en-US" style="line-height: 14.2667px; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;inancial statements presented herein are prepared in accordance with the accounting requirements of the FERC, as set forth in the applicable Uniform System of Accounts and published accounting releases, which is a comprehensive basis of accounting other than accounting principles generally accepted in the United States of America (&amp;quot;GAAP&amp;quot;). T&lt;span style="color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); float: none; display: inline !important"&gt;he most significant differences between GAAP and the financial statements presented herein are: (1) subsidiaries are reflected on the equity method whereas GAAP requires that all majority-owned subsidiaries be consolidated (2) classification of certain accounts on the balance sheet, statement of income and the statement of cash flows and (3) use of FERC approved depreciation rates.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 13.2pt; margin-bottom: 8pt; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); text-align: justify; line-height: 17.12px"&gt;&lt;span lang="en-US" style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; text-decoration: none; line-height: 14.2667px"&gt;NOTE B - SUMMARY OF SIGNIFICANT ACCOUNTING POLICIES AND OTHER MATTERS&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span lang="en-US" style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; text-decoration: none; line-height: 14.2667px"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); line-height: 17.12px"&gt;&lt;span lang="en-US" style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; text-decoration: underline; line-height: 14.2667px"&gt;Use of Estimates&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); line-height: 17.12px"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; background-color: initial"&gt;The preparation of financial statements requires management to make estimates and assumptions that affect the reported amounts of assets and liabilities and disclosure of contingent assets and liabilities at the date of the financial statements and reported amounts of revenues and expenses during the reporting period. Actual results could differ from those estimates.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); line-height: 17.12px"&gt;&lt;span lang="en-US" style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; text-decoration: underline; line-height: 14.2667px"&gt;Cash and Cash Equivalents&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); line-height: 17.12px"&gt;&lt;span lang="en-US" style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-weight: normal; font-style: normal; text-decoration: none; line-height: 14.2667px"&gt;Cash equivalents consist of highly liquid investments, which are readily convertible into cash and have original maturities of three months or less. The cash deposits and temporary cash investments are placed with high credit quality financial institutions. At times, PEP's cash and cash equivalents may be uninsured or in deposit accounts that exceed the Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation insurance limit.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); line-height: 17.12px"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&lt;b style="font-weight: bolder; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;Property, Plant and Equipment&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); line-height: normal"&gt;&lt;span lang="en-US" style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-weight: normal; font-style: normal; text-decoration: none"&gt;PEP capitalizes expenditures related to property, plant and equipment that have a useful life greater than one year for (1) assets purchased or constructed; (2) existing assets that are replaced or improved; or (3) land regardless of cost. During construction, PEP capitalizes direct costs, such as labor, materials, and overhead. PEP records property, plant and equipment at its original cost. For financial reporting purposes, depreciation is computed on a composite straight-line method at rates based on the expected economic lives of the various classes of assets.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); line-height: normal"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&lt;br style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small" /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); line-height: normal"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&lt;b style="font-weight: bolder; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;Accounts Receivable and Allowance for Credit Losses&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); line-height: normal"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); line-height: normal"&gt;&lt;span lang="en-US" style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-weight: normal; font-style: normal; text-decoration: none"&gt;Accounts receivables are carried at the amount owed by customers less an allowance for credit losses. PEP evaluates the collectability of accounts receivables based on review of a specific customer's ability to meet its financial obligation or as a result of changes in the overall aging of accounts receivables.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); line-height: normal"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); line-height: normal"&gt;&lt;span lang="en-US" style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-weight: normal; font-style: normal; text-decoration: none"&gt;PEP's allowance for credit losses was $ 2.2 million and nil as of December 31, 2025 and 2024&lt;span style="color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); display: inline !important; float: none"&gt;, respectively.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); line-height: normal"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); line-height: normal"&gt;&lt;b style="font-weight: bolder; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;Revenue Recognition&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); line-height: normal"&gt;&lt;b style="font-weight: bolder; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); line-height: normal"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-weight: bold; background-color: initial"&gt;Contract Balances with Customers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); line-height: normal"&gt;&lt;span lang="en-US" style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-weight: normal; font-style: normal; text-decoration: none"&gt;PEP satisfies its obligations by transferring goods or services in exchange for consideration from customers. The timing of performance may differ from the timing that the associated consideration is received from the customer, thus resulting in the recognition of a contract liability.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); line-height: normal"&gt;&lt;br style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); line-height: normal"&gt;PEP recognizes a contract liability if the customer's payment of consideration precedes PEP's fulfillment of the performance obligations. Certain contracts contain provisions requiring customers to pay a fixed fee for a right to use PEP's assets but allow customers to apply such fees against services to be provided at a future point in time. These amounts are reflected as deferred revenue until the customer applies the deficiency fees to services provided or becomes unable to use the fees as payment for future services due to expiration of the contractual period the fees can be applied or physical inability of the customer to utilize the fees due to capacity constraints.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); line-height: normal"&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: bold; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&lt;br style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small" /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); line-height: normal"&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: bold; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;Performance Obligations&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); line-height: normal"&gt;&lt;span lang="en-US" style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-weight: normal; font-style: normal; text-decoration: none"&gt;At contract inception, PEP assesses the goods and services promised in its contracts with customers and identifies a performance obligation for each promise to transfer a good or service that is distinct. Revenue is recognized when (or as) the performance obligations are satisfied, that is, when the customer obtains control of the good or service. P&lt;/span&gt;EP generally does not own the crude oil that it transports or stores.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); line-height: normal"&gt;&lt;br style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); line-height: normal"&gt;&lt;span lang="en-US" style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; text-decoration: underline"&gt;Income Taxes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); line-height: normal"&gt;&lt;br style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); line-height: normal"&gt;PEP is a limited liability company that passes the federal income liability through to its members and does not recognize this liability on its financial statements. PEP is subject to the Revised Texas Franchise Tax, enacted by the State of Texas in May 2006.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); line-height: normal"&gt;&lt;span style="background-color: initial; font-weight: bold; text-align: justify; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&lt;br style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small" /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); line-height: normal"&gt;&lt;b style="font-weight: bolder; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;Environmental Remediation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); line-height: normal"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class="_Normal_" style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 1rem; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); text-align: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="background-color: initial; text-align: inherit; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;PEP accrues environmental remediation costs for work at identified sites where an assessment has indicated that cleanup costs are probable and reasonably estimable. Such accruals are undiscounted and are based on currently available information, estimated timing of remedial actions and related inflation assumptions, existing technology and presently enacted laws and regulations. If a range of probable environmental cleanup costs exists for an identified site, the minimum of the range is accrued unless some other point or points in the range are more likely, in which case the most likely amount in this range is accrued.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class="_Normal_" style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 1rem; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1)"&gt;&lt;b style="font-weight: bolder"&gt;NOTE C - COMMITMENT AND CONTINGENCIES:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 1rem; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1)"&gt;&lt;span style="background-color: initial; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;PEP m&lt;span style="color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); float: none; display: inline !important"&gt;ay be subject to various legal proceedings and claims that arise in the ordinary course of business. In the opinion of management, the amount of any ultimate liability with respect to any such actions will not materially affect the company's financial position or results of operation.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); line-height: normal"&gt;&lt;span lang="en-US" style="color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-style: normal; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; text-decoration: none; font-weight: bold; line-height: 14.2667px"&gt;NOTE D - RELATED PARTY TRANSACTIONS:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); line-height: normal"&gt;&lt;span lang="en-US" style="color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-style: normal; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; text-decoration: none; font-weight: bold; line-height: 14.2667px"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); line-height: normal"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline"&gt;Operating Management Fees&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); line-height: normal"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); line-height: normal"&gt;PEP pays Energy Transfer an annual fixed operating fee as reimbursement for providing certain services including business development, legal services, accounting and financial reporting, human resource services, and other as defined in the operating agreement. The fixed operating fee is escalated annually and is Energy Transfer's sole reimbursement and compensation for any allocation of Energy Transfer's or its affiliates' overhead related to the services. The fixed operating fee was $6.2 million and $5.9 million for the years ended December 31, 2025 and 2024, respectively.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); line-height: normal"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; text-align: justify; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); line-height: normal"&gt;&lt;span lang="en-US" style="color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-style: normal; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; text-decoration: none; font-weight: bold; line-height: 14.2667px"&gt;NOTE E - REGULATORY MATTERS:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; text-align: justify; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); line-height: normal"&gt;&lt;span lang="en-US" style="color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-style: normal; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; text-decoration: none; font-weight: bold; line-height: 14.2667px"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; text-align: justify; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); line-height: normal"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-style: normal; font-weight: 700; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); float: none; display: inline !important"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial; font-size: 13.3333px; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); float: none; display: inline !important"&gt;In accordance with the Order Denying Rehearing, Denying Petition and Granting Remedies in Docket No. RM20-14-004 (&amp;quot;Order&amp;quot;) issued on November 20, 2025 footnote 111, we have determined that rebillings, as permitted in that Order, are not distortive. In accordance with the rebillings, $5.0 million and $2.2 million have been included in operating revenues and bad debt expense, respectively, in the accompanying income statement for the year ended December 31,2025.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; text-align: justify; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); line-height: normal"&gt;&lt;br style="color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal" /&gt;  &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class="_Normal_" style="margin: 0 0 1rem; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); line-height: 18.4px; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial; font-size: 13.3333px; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); float: none; display: inline !important"&gt;&lt;b style="font-weight: bold"&gt;NOTE F - SUPPLEMENTAL CASH FLOW INFORMATION:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); line-height: normal"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; background-color: initial"&gt;Accrued capital expenditures as of December 31, 2025 and 2024 were $0.7 million and $ 1.7 million, respectively.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; text-align: justify; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); line-height: normal"&gt;&lt;span lang="en-US" style="color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-style: normal; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; text-decoration: none; font-weight: bold; line-height: 14.2667px"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); line-height: normal"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); line-height: normal"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-style: normal; font-weight: 700; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); display: inline !important; float: none"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; background-color: initial"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; background-color: initial"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock>
